  "summary": "Chicago police ran over 23,000 Flock license plate camera searches between May and July 2026, accessing the network through a city agreement rather than a direct Flock contract. The article situates this within Illinois's 2023 ALPR privacy law, an ongoing state investigation of Flock, pending federal and state legislation, and contrasting suburban decisions by Evanston and Bartlett to pull back from Flock.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Chicago police officers ran more than 23,000 searches through Flock Safety's license plate camera database between May and July 2026, accessing the privately owned network through a city agreement rather than a direct contract with Flock Safety.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Illinois Secretary of State Alexi Giannoulias began an investigation into Flock Safety in August 2025 amid allegations that the company had allowed U.S. Customs and Border Protection and out-of-state police to access Illinois plate data in violation of state law",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Prosecutors charged two former suburban Chicago police officers with official misconduct in October for allegedly misusing Flock camera networks and law enforcement databases to conduct unauthorized personal searches",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    }
  ],
